  "goodToKnow": "Rügen means to reprimand or rebuke, a formal word: jemanden scharf rügen. Die Rüge is a reprimand. The Deutscher Presserat (German Press Council) issues public Rügen to newspapers that break the press code, and Bild has received more than any other. Everyday words are tadeln or ermahnen. Unrelated, Rügen is also Germany's largest island, in the Baltic Sea, famous for its white chalk cliffs painted by Caspar David Friedrich."
